Practically you won't go for "perfect safety", rather you're deciding
the required quality of safety on what you have and what might happen
or appear on the level you are.
Close to perfect safety might be the already mentioned icebox on an
Elbereth burned square and covered by a boulder and a cursed item.
But typically you can drop your loot even unprotected adjacent to
the stairs where you leave the level, or only slightly protected by
a non-permanent E-word, or quite good protected in a container.
If demands are higher choose from any option combination enumerated
in the "perfect" case; a boulder, or any container, or enduring
engravings, or, a cursed item on top. Each of those options serves
some purpose to protect the square.
Better locations can be (but not necessarily are) niches, corners
of a room, dead ends of corridors. Some levels, especially branches
are often used for stashes; first of all the first level of Sokoban,
or the entry chamber of Ludios, or on the Home quest level adjacent
to the portal, later in the game Vlad's tower.

